ef 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444362 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444362 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186444352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444362 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "90ab5756-be68-58c5-811b-5048edcd87d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444363 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444363 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444363 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444363 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444363 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444363 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444363 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444363 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186444335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444363 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d5476fb6-80da-5fb0-9202-81c168d50130" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444365 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444365 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107272" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444365 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444365 #edb/ref 1071 "Find an eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}-23 & 6 \\\\ 8 & -10\\end{aligned}]$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-7.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444365 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "59c071a9-0532-5356-9a7b-f9737214176f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444365 #edb/ref 1074 "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\,\\lambda =-7.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}-23 & 6 \\\\ 8 & -10\\end{aligned}]-(-7)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-16 & 6 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the homogeneous system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-16{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-16 & 6 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-16 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. \n\nFrom the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-16{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{3}{8}{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFinally, setting ${x}_{2}=8,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444368 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444368 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "37c3a8ed-fc50-5c91-b1c0-b7f217640868" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444368 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186444365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444369 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444369 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3f94626d-4241-5985-b60b-4e7b51ef0b27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444369 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186444367 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444370 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444370 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a5b46e54-d2f8-5763-b2eb-1a4ff3c797a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444370 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186444366 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444371 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186444370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444371 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cf52d8f0-fe30-5018-947f-1ec4c11f7b2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444371 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444372 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "db002